# `JavaScript` code example

It is assumed that you have a recent version of `node.js` and its `npm` package manager
installed. The generated code has a dependency on
[Confluent JavaScript Client for Apache Kafka](https://docs.confluent.io/kafka-clients/javascript/current/overview.html).

To run the example scripts, first install the `@confluentinc/kafka-javascript` client library 
(if it is not already installed):

```shell
> cd {{proxy-name}}-example-javascript
> npm install "@confluentinc/kafka-javascript"
...
```

List all Kafka topics that you have read access to.

```shell
> node list-topics
scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}
...
```

Send some messages to Kafka topic `scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}`. Use `ctrl-c` to stop the program.

```shell
> node producer scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}
{{proxy-name}}-producer-javascript: 1782301678
{{proxy-name}}-producer-javascript: 1782301679
{{proxy-name}}-producer-javascript: 1782301680
{{proxy-name}}-producer-javascript: 1782301681
{{proxy-name}}-producer-javascript: 1782301682
^CSIGINT
```

Consume records from the same topic. Again, use `ctrl-c` to stop the program.

```shell
> node consumer scratch.my-topic.{{tenant}}
0:3099 {{proxy-name}}-producer-javascript: 1782301678
0:3100 {{proxy-name}}-producer-javascript: 1782301679
0:3101 {{proxy-name}}-producer-javascript: 1782301680
0:3102 {{proxy-name}}-producer-javascript: 1782301681
0:3103 {{proxy-name}}-producer-javascript: 1782301682
^CSIGINT
```
